If only nethack was implemented with an embedded scripting language, it
could be trivial to add variety like thousand different door types. As
it is, they just stick more and more stuff directly into the C code
(even the t-shirt comments are in there, for heaven's sake!). Since
nethack already has a lot of variety, the executable is huge, and now
it seems to me that the dev team rejects perfectly reasonable patches
out of size concerns.

It's probably too late to change now, of course. It would require a
full rewrite. Yet I wonder if there are any roguelikes which are fully
scriptable?



